<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of the Franks</h1><p class="st-meta">936 CE – 987 CE (approx.) · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The great Robertian principality between the Seine and the Loire whose dukes overshadowed the last Carolingian kings and became the Capetian dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Robertian family had led the defence of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/neustria">Neustria</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> since <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-strong">Robert the Strong</a> in the 860s, and two of its members, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-of-france">Odo</a> and Robert I, had briefly been kings. In 936 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-the-great">Hugh the Great</a> helped restore the Carolingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-of-france">Louis IV</a> and was recognised as 'duke of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>', second only to the king.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-the-great">Hugh the Great</a> held counties and lay abbacies around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbey-of-saint-martin-of-tours">Saint-Martin of Tours</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basilica-of-saint-denis">Saint-Denis</a>, giving him more land and men than the king. He controlled royal successions and dealt as an equal with the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a> inherited the title in 956.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the last Carolingian king, Louis V, died in 987, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a> king. The duchy's lands became the royal domain of the new Capetian <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>, which his descendants ruled for eight centuries.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 936 CE – 987 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.33%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>936 CE – 987 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hugh the Great, Hugh Capet</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of France, Robertian march</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=962&amp;focus=duchy-of-the-franks" aria-label="Duchy of the Franks on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of the Franks lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=962&amp;focus=duchy-of-the-franks">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
